{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5jkkwfS1KP6GqvaQiER","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `Shipment.kt:9`\n- ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED: `Shipment.kt:23`\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:22` (currently has create, getById, list endpoints only)\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:11` (simple in-memory store with save, findById, existsById)\n- Error handling pattern: ApiException hierarchy at `ApiExceptions.kt:11` with ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ErrorCode enum: `ApiError.kt:31` (currently has ORDER_*, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14` (converts exceptions to ApiError envelope)\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw exceptions (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) rather than returning error responses\n- Conflicts use HTTP 409 with ConflictException\n- Not found uses HTTP 404 with ResourceNotFoundException\n- All errors wrapped in ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on both success and error cases\n- Status codes checked with `.isCreated()`, `.isOk()`, `.isConflict()`, `.isNotFound()`\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests for confirm endpoint\n3. `ApiError.kt` - add new ErrorCode for invalid shipment status (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if endpoint path conflicts or state handling is wrong\n- Not handling idempotent retry properly (confirm when already confirmed should succeed)\n- Status code mismatch for cancelled shipment error\n\n**Open questions:** None identified; requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code to the ErrorCode enum for when a shipment is in an invalid state for confirmation (e.g., CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new method `confirmShipment()` decorated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException (404) if not found\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and persists the new status` - create S-1, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED\n   - `retry confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds` - confirm once, confirm again, verify still CONFIRMED and returns 200\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` - create and manually set to CANCELLED, confirm attempt, verify 409 and error code\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` - confirm non-existent ID, verify 404 and error code\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\nI considered not adding a new ErrorCode and reusing SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS or using a generic VALIDATION_FAILED code, but that would violate semantic accuracy and consistency with the existing error pattern (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND are specific). The new code is necessary and minimal.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: Confirming CREATED shipment*\n- Read: Repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns Shipment with status=CREATED\n- Modify: status changed to CONFIRMED\n- Write: Repository.save(modified shipment)\n- Return: HTTP 200 with updated Shipment JSON\n\n*Case 2: Retrying confirmation on CONFIRMED shipment*\n- Read: Repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns Shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n- No modification, no write\n- Return: HTTP 200 with unchanged Shipment JSON (idempotent)\n\n*Case 3: Confirming CANCELLED shipment*\n- Read: Repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns Shipment with status=CANCELLED\n- Throw: ConflictException with ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n- Return: HTTP 409 with ApiError envelope containing error code and message\n\n*Case 4: Confirming non-existent shipment*\n- Read: Repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns null\n- Throw: ResourceNotFoundException with ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n- Return: HTTP 404 with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 verifies the primary success case: CREATED → CONFIRMED transition persists\n- Test 2 verifies idempotence: second confirm on CONFIRMED shipment succeeds silently\n- Test 3 verifies error handling for invalid state: CANCELLED shipment rejects with 409\n- Test 4 verifies error handling for missing resource: non-existent ID returns 404\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1380,"cache_read_input_tokens":18235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1380},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"831a2c16-68c1-4275-8021-58764d8cd7c3","uuid":"9232aa4a-fc69-4501-8e8d-09b7f697b4e4","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:58:49.012Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5jkkTteEK5UVDFGpq6J"}
